From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(resource-packs): decode Bedrock TGA textures

Some Bedrock packs supply entity textures as uncompressed or RLE true-color TGA rather than PNG or JPEG. Decode both supported true-color forms when loading a texture and retain their origin and alpha information so pack conversion can use those assets.

Follow the stb_image TGA loader that the native 1.26.60.5 client embeds
(its "bad palette" and "unknown image type" messages are in the binary).
Besides true color, it reads grayscale and color-mapped images, plain or
run-length encoded, with 15/16-bit 5-5-5 color. Lifeboat ships its
vehicle textures as type 9 color-mapped TGAs, and the true-color-only
decoder failed the whole pack conversion and disconnected the player.
Like stb_image, an index outside the palette uses the first entry.

stb_image accepts each TGA side up to its 16-bit field, so a fixed
4096 x 4096 bound rejected textures that native loads. Use the
heap-relative image decoding bound that PNG and JPEG textures share.
A few run-length packets can still declare a 65535 x 65535 image, and
the regression rejects it before allocating pixels.

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/api/resourcepack/content/Content.java b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/api/resourcepack/content/Content.java
index f8805725d6d3e57b7d625fe74a57088a240ce763..6cae87972e12fb66be66d939b92b9606432a8891 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/api/resourcepack/content/Content.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/api/resourcepack/content/Content.java
@@ -141,7 +141,7 @@ public abstract class Content {
     }
 
     public LazyImage getShortnameImage(final String path) {
-        final String fullPath = this.getFullPath(path, "png", "jpg");
+        final String fullPath = this.getFullPath(path, "png", "jpg", "tga");
         return fullPath == null ? null : this.getImage(fullPath);
     }
 
@@ -153,11 +153,12 @@ public abstract class Content {
 
         final boolean isPng = bytes.length > 8 && bytes[0] == (byte) 0x89 && bytes[1] == (byte) 0x50 && bytes[2] == (byte) 0x4E && bytes[3] == (byte) 0x47 && bytes[4] == (byte) 0x0D && bytes[5] == (byte) 0x0A && bytes[6] == (byte) 0x1A && bytes[7] == (byte) 0x0A;
         final boolean isJpg = bytes.length > 2 && bytes[0] == (byte) 0xFF && bytes[1] == (byte) 0xD8 && bytes[2] == (byte) 0xFF;
-        if (!isPng && !isJpg) {
+        final boolean isTga = path.endsWith(".tga");
+        if (!isPng && !isJpg && !isTga) {
             return null;
         }
 
-        return new LazyImage(bytes, isPng ? "png" : "jpg");
+        return new LazyImage(bytes, isPng ? "png" : isJpg ? "jpg" : "tga");
     }
 
     public boolean putPngImage(final String path, final LazyImage image) {
@@ -214,6 +215,10 @@ public abstract class Content {
         /** Returns null when no reader supports the format or the image data cannot be decoded. */
         public BufferedImage getImage() {
             if (this.image == null && !this.undecodable) {
+                if (this.format.equals("tga")) {
+                    this.image = TgaImage.read(this.bytes);
+                    return this.image;
+                }
                 try {
                     this.image = decode(this.bytes);
                 } catch (final IOException e) {
diff --git a/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/api/resourcepack/content/TgaImage.java b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/api/resourcepack/content/TgaImage.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..51e0b21cebac3821b7dd43daeb4fed2556a31051
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/main/java/net/raphimc/viabedrock/api/resourcepack/content/TgaImage.java
@@ -0,0 +1,154 @@
+/*
+ * This file is part of ViaBedrock - https://github.com/RaphiMC/ViaBedrock
+ * Copyright (C) 2023-2026 RK_01/RaphiMC and contributors
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
